---
layout: room.njk
description: "Affirmable: the most beautiful way to create and curate your own affirmations, on iPhone and iPad. On the App Store."
lede: "The most beautiful way to create and curate your own affirmations, on your cards, on your Home Screen, and through your day. The original came out in 2014; Affirmable 2.0 is rebuilt from the ground up."
privacyLine: "Your affirmations live on your iPhone and iPad and in your own iCloud. Individuate can’t see them."
distribution: "App Store"
affirmations:
  - "This moment will never come again, so I give it my whole heart."
  - "I am allowed to rest."
  - "Water is soft, yet it wears away stone. My gentleness is my strength."
  - "I welcome my feelings as guests, and let them leave when they are ready."
  - "Fall seven times, stand up eight."
  - "I bend like bamboo, and I do not break."
  - "Like mended pottery, I am more beautiful where I have healed."
  - "I speak to myself as kindly as I would to a friend."
  - "Every day is a good day."
  - "I may go slowly, but I do not stop."
  - "My thoughts pass like clouds, and I remain."
  - "Today I take one small step, and that is enough."
  - "I am braver than I feel right now."
  - "I do not need to be finished to be worthy."
  - "I have enough, and I am enough."
---
{%- from "macros.njk" import shuffle -%}
<section class="exhibits" aria-label="In this room">
  <div class="affirmation-wall">
    <p class="affirmation" id="affirmation" aria-live="polite">{{ affirmations[0] }}</p>
    <div>
      <button type="button" class="another" id="another" hidden>{{ shuffle() | safe }}Another one</button>
    </div>
    <script type="application/json" id="affirmations">{{ affirmations | dump | safe }}</script>
  </div>
  <div class="affirm-copy">
    <p class="wall-copy">Affirmable 2.0 comes with thirty-six affirmations, new and very old, drawn from many traditions and mixed so no two neighbors come from the same one.</p>
    <p class="wall-copy soft">Everything you keep syncs through your own iCloud, so your affirmations follow you from device to device and never pass through Individuate.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="diptychs">
    <section class="diptych" aria-labelledby="d-cards">
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <div class="panels">
          <img src="/assets/img/affirmable-card.webp" alt="An Affirmable card in the New York typeface: Before enlightenment, chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment, chop wood, carry water. Buttons beneath for share, read aloud, shuffle, and your affirmations." width="600" height="1304" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <img src="/assets/img/affirmable-typeface.webp" alt="An Affirmable card in the handwritten Noteworthy typeface: Today I take one small step, and that is enough." width="600" height="1304" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
        <figcaption><b>One at a time</b>Cards in New York and in Noteworthy.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="copy">
        <h2 id="d-cards">Cards</h2>
        <p>Each affirmation gets a card to itself. Tap shuffle, or shake your iPhone or iPad, for another. Tap the speaker to hear it read aloud, in your Spoken Content voice or your own Personal Voice.</p>
        <p>Set your cards in New York, Optima, Noteworthy, or Rounded.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="diptych" aria-labelledby="d-list">
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <div class="panels">
          <img src="/assets/img/affirmable-list.webp" alt="The Affirmations list, with a tick beside each affirmation shown on the cards and an empty circle beside the two that are hidden." width="600" height="1304" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <img src="/assets/img/affirmable-writing.webp" alt="The New Affirmation sheet with I finish what I start, one page at a time. typed in, a Remind Me Daily option, and the keyboard." width="600" height="1304" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
        <figcaption><b>Your list, and a new one</b>Ticked affirmations appear on your cards.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="copy">
        <h2 id="d-list">Your list</h2>
        <p>Flip from the cards to your list. Tick the affirmations you want on your cards; the rest wait, unticked, until you want them. Put them in any order you like.</p>
        <p>Write your own by typing, or tap the keyboard’s microphone and say it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="diptych" aria-labelledby="d-day">
      <figure class="exhibit">
        <div class="panels">
          <img src="/assets/img/affirmable-widget.webp" alt="A large Affirmable widget on an iPhone Home Screen: I welcome my feelings as guests, and let them leave when they are ready. Shuffle and next buttons sit in its corner." width="600" height="1304" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <img src="/assets/img/affirmable-reminders.webp" alt="Affirmable’s settings: reminders for two affirmations at 7:00 AM and 1:00 PM, a Daily Mix at 7:30 PM, the four typefaces, and the read-aloud voice." width="600" height="1304" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
        <figcaption><b>Through the day</b>A Home Screen widget, and reminders.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="copy">
        <h2 id="d-day">Through the day</h2>
        <p>Keep an affirmation on your Home Screen in a small, medium, or large widget. It changes through the day, and you can shuffle it or step to the next one without opening the app.</p>
        <p>Be reminded of a particular affirmation every day, or set a Daily Mix that brings one from your cards at the times you pick.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="write-own">
    <h2>Write <b>your own</b></h2>
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="wall-copy">Affirmable comes with thirty-six affirmations to choose from. An affordable one-time purchase unlocks writing and editing: add your own, edit or delete any in your list, and get reminders. No subscription. It works on all your devices and is shared with your family.</p>
      <p class="wall-copy soft">Had the original Affirmable? Writing and editing are free for you, and the affirmations you kept come along when you update to 2.0.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="apple-tech">
    <h2>Full Support of Apple Technologies</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Light and Dark Mode.</b> Warm paper by day, dark paper at night, and an app icon in light, dark, and tinted.</li>
      <li><b>VoiceOver.</b> Affirmations, buttons, and settings are labeled, with hints where a gesture isn’t obvious.</li>
      <li><b>Dynamic Type.</b> Affirmations and controls grow with your text size. At the largest sizes, touch and hold a button to see its name.</li>
      <li><b>Reduce Motion.</b> Cards change without animation when Reduce Motion is on.</li>
      <li><b>Spoken Content and Personal Voice.</b> Hear any affirmation read aloud in the voice you chose for your device, or in your own.</li>
      <li><b>Dictation.</b> Say a new affirmation instead of typing it.</li>
      <li><b>Interactive widgets.</b> Small, medium, and large, changing every hour, every three hours, or every day. Shuffle or step ahead right on your Home Screen, and see the small one in StandBy.</li>
      <li><b>Notifications.</b> Reminders arrive at the times you pick, and on a paired Apple Watch.</li>
      <li><b>iCloud.</b> Your affirmations sync privately between your iPhone and iPad.</li>
      <li><b>Family Sharing.</b> One purchase unlocks writing and editing for everyone in your family.</li>
      <li><b>iPhone and iPad.</b> Portrait or landscape, and shake either one for a new affirmation.</li>
      <li><b>Liquid Glass.</b> The round buttons along the bottom are Liquid Glass, new in iOS 26.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
